#:seon.wake{:listen
            [:boolean
             {:description
              "On a ref attribute: Datahike `listen` reports its assertions and the entity the datom points at is the agent to wake. Answeredness is derived from the transaction `:t` the datom carries, so nothing is copied onto the wake and nothing references it back. THE DATOM IS ASSERTED ONCE AND NEVER RETRACTED-AND-REASSERTED: a reassertion moves the wake's `:t` forward and re-opens a paid turn."}],
            :opens-turn?
            [:boolean
             {:description
              "Whether an unanswered wake on this attribute opens a turn. Declared false, the wake still routes and still reaches the agent's next context; it never causes a model call on its own — a schedule fire is the example."}],
            :inside
            [:boolean
             {:description
              "On any attribute: its presence on a wake entity marks that wake as the population's OWN activity, so it does not reset the agent's turn bound. An agent-sent message, a fault routed to its steward, and an effect the agent itself requested are all inside; a human message and a firing are not. THE ANCHOR IS THE LATEST OUTSIDE WAKE'S OWN `:t`."}],
            :attribute
            [:qualified-keyword
             {:description
              "Which listened attribute carried one wake datom."}],
            :t
            [:int
             {:min 0
              :description
              "The transaction `:t` Datahike stamped on one wake datom. Answeredness compares it against a turn's own `:t`; nothing stores either."}],
            :unanswered
            [:map
             {:description
              "One wake as `seon.turn/unanswered-wakes` returns it: the entity carrying the datom, which attribute carried it, and its transaction. The message keys are present only when the wake is a message."}
             [:db/id :int]
             [:seon.wake/attribute :seon.wake/attribute]
             [:seon.wake/t :seon.wake/t]
             [:seon.message/id
              {:optional true}
              :seon.message/id]
]}
